648 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 649 0 R/Alt(A line plot of the largest phase difference between a low-level model and the structure, in degrees from 0 to 180, against how far the resonance has moved, in half-power bandwidths from 0 to 5. A single blue solid curve, 2 arctan of the shift, rises steeply from 0 and bends over toward 180 degrees, passing 53 degrees at 0.5, 90 degrees at 1 and 127 degrees at 2. A dashed black horizontal line at 90 degrees is labeled "90 degrees: a one-channel correction stops converging". Three open orange markers on the curve, with labels, show where a 1 percent shift falls for a Q of 25 (0.25 bandwidth, 28 degrees), 50 (0.5, 53 degrees) and 100 (1.0, 90 degrees).)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[15]/Pg 1008 0 R>>
endobj
